# QUICKSTART — first run against the 0.1 release

Release 0.1 is the minimal self-bootstrap closure: the committed wasm
seed, the `rsdc`/`rsc` source closure, the runtime and these documents.
There is no `raisin` command, no modules and no execution layer in 0.1 —
the first run is the seed recipe itself. Every claim names its source.
This document will change in later versions (0.11+).

## 20 to 45 minutes: rebuild the compilers from the seed

On a clean Linux x86-64 checkout — or the source archive extracted
into a fresh directory (`mkdir rsd-src && tar -xf rsd-src.tar -C
rsd-src`; the archive's members sit at its top level) — with GCC,
GNU binutils, coreutils, Bash, curl and tar, and no Lean, elan, lake,
Node or OCaml on PATH, run the pinned recipe:

```sh
env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin bash --noprofile --norc
# then the commands of bootstrap/seed/stage-14274/README.md
```

(The measured spread is 1154.8 s on the recorded perf host to 2043 s
on a 4-vCPU Debian 12 guest — `release/docs/PERF-RECORD.tsv`.)

The recipe fetches pinned WABT 1.0.42 and runtime sources (digests in
`bootstrap/seed/stage-14274/WABT{,-RUNTIME}-SHA256SUMS`), translates the
two seed executors to C, builds them, and runs all four compiler calls
in the CPU executables. It rebuilds both RSCM files and both Wasm
files byte-identical to the committed seeds and exits 0 — the recipe's
wall and peak are recorded per version in `release/docs/PERF-RECORD.tsv`.

## What just happened

`bootstrap/seed/stage-14274/rsdc.wasm` (sha256 `97e549715d04…ef5933`) read
the whole-module input `sources/rsdc.rsd` and emitted an RSCM file
matching the fixpoint digest; `stage-14274/rsc.wasm` (sha256
`3425f3e9b1b2…d7b82d`) lowered both RSCM files to Wasm matching the
committed seeds (`stage-14274/README.md`, `REBUILT-SHA256SUMS`,
`SHA256SUMS`). The 54 source members the seeds were cut from are pinned
by sha256 in `stage-14274/SOURCE-MEMBERS-SHA256SUMS` — `sha256sum -c`
verifies them against the checkout.

## Compiling a source

The rebuilt executors are the compiler:
`$out/rsdc/run rsdc <source.rsd> <out.rscm> 0 cons` compiles, and
`$out/rsc/run rsc <file.rscm> <out.wasm> 14274 cons` lowers
(`stage-14274/README.md`, the `rebuild_root` command lines). The
inputs the recipe demonstrates are the two whole-module sources
`sources/{rsdc,rsc}.rsd` — "the exact RSD byte streams" of the
seed cut, including generated runtime definitions
(`stage-14274/README.md`); the grammar those sources are written in
is `release/docs/LANGUAGE`, whose probe table refuses `import`,
`theorem`, `axiom`, `class`, `abbrev`, `variable`, `opaque`, `by`
(all err=1).

## Not in 0.1

Modules (`import`), the `raisin`/`raisinc` binaries and their
example programs, the 9P execution layer's device servers,
theorem checking, the elaborator, the `.rsm`/`.rsj` surfaces, the RSX
entry and the application suites are named 0.1x work
(`release/MANIFEST.md`, `release/docs/OVERVIEW`).

